From 910d0b94edc0174bac10f3cc808f9fbe24ac283d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 20:47:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat: edit a session after it has been created
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A session's title, date, length and description could only be set once, at
the moment it was added. A class moved by a week, or a title typed in a
hurry, meant deleting the session and building it again — taking its
slides, quiz and assignment with it.

Each session now has an Edit button covering all four, alongside the
links and facilitator that were already editable.

The date conversion lives in @workspace/domain with tests, because the
obvious one-liner is wrong outside UTC: it would have shown a 6pm Lagos
class as 5pm and, on an untouched save, actually moved it. A test also
caught an empty minutes box turning a class into five minutes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
