From b615424056c6595504e37f068bee626f93b7e0b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 21:41:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] feat: a waitlist instead of open sign-up, and People as
 staff only

Anybody could sign up, land in the Lab on no programme at all, and sit in
the People list beside the facilitators. That is fixed at the source.

Joining is now a waitlist: name, address, which programme. No account is
created. /sign-up shows the real form only when the address carries a
Clerk invitation ticket; everyone else is told the Lab runs by invitation
and sent to the waitlist. Accounts come from invitations, and an invited
learner is enrolled on arrival, so an account with no programme can no
longer happen.

People now lists only the people who run the Lab: administrators, and
facilitators shown with the programmes they teach. Learners moved to
Enrollments, arranged by programme with each cohort's count against its
places, because a cohort is the unit an admin actually works in.

A super admin tier sits above admin, because appointing staff is the one
decision the people it affects must not be able to make. The first account
holds it; on a Lab that predates the tier, the first admin is treated as
super admin until one is appointed, so nobody is locked out. Only a super
admin changes roles or invites an admin, and the last one cannot be
removed.

An invited admin is raised from our own invitation record rather than from
anything Clerk carries, so the rule that link-borne metadata cannot make
an admin still holds exactly as written, and nothing at all can make a
super admin.

Also: the accounts already stranded on no programme are listed in
Enrollments for you to deal with by hand, and the two public forms now
share one rate limiter rather than a copy each.

Needs the schema update: one new table and one new column.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
