From fbf259bac5c65c4f5708fda481d29027791a5fc2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 07:13:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] fix: tell people when an admin puts them on a programme
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adding somebody who already has an account enrolled them and said nothing
to them. They get no invitation — an invitation is for people with no
account — so they found out by chance, or not at all. An admin testing the
roster tool with two of their own addresses met exactly this and
reasonably read it as the feature being broken.

They are now emailed that they have a place. The outcome line in the
console says so too, rather than the ambiguous 'enrolled directly'.

Also fixes every link in every enrolment email. The address was built from
Replit's environment variables and a hard-coded old base path, neither of
which exists on Railway, so 'Open my dashboard' was a bare path that opens
nothing from an inbox. It now uses APP_BASE_URL, the same setting the
invitation links already use.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
